Keeper auth / caller-allowlist / pause branches live in KeeperExecutorBase.tree.

QueueKeeperExecutor::constructor(address registry_)
└── It should default policy knobs (minBatchAge, maxUsersPerUpkeep, GAS_INTENSIVE_ACTION_*) and version "2.0.0-gelato"

QueueKeeperExecutor::perform(uint8 action, bytes params) — called by the allowlisted Gelato proxy
├── Given action is PriceBatch
│   ├── It should price the batch when it is mature and unpriced
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded otherwise
├── Given action is ProcessRequests
│   ├── It should process affordable requests in [startIndex, startIndex+count)
│   ├── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded when the claimed range exceeds affordableRequests
│   └── It should pull-over-push: credits land in amm.claimableBalances, not held by the executor
├── Given action is AdvanceCursor
│   ├── It should advance the cursor past settled/expired batches
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded when nothing is skippable
├── Given action is None / unknown
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorUnknownAction
└── Given msg.sender is not allowlisted
    └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorUnauthorizedCaller / KeeperExecutorNoAllowedCallers

QueueKeeperExecutor::checker()
├── It should return (false, "") when queueUpkeepStatus() is None
└── It should return (true, abi.encodeCall(this.perform, ...)) mirroring queueUpkeepStatus()
    (execPayload is the exact calldata perform accepts — verified by executing it as the proxy)

QueueKeeperExecutor::queueUpkeepStatus()
├── It should prefer PriceBatch over ProcessRequests over AdvanceCursor (priority order)
├── It should return None while the current batch is below minBatchAge
└── It should return None when the executor / Controller is paused

QueueKeeperExecutor::nextLiveBatchIdToProcess()
├── It should not skip an unpriced current batch (it can still receive requests)
├── It should skip a priced batch with zero unprocessed users (fully settled)
└── It should skip a priced batch past MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME (escape hatch)

QueueKeeperExecutor::affordableRequests(uint256 _batchId)
└── It should count only requests the Controller can afford at live prices

QueueKeeperExecutor::setMinBatchAge / setMaxUsersPerUpkeep / advanceBatchCursor
└── It should enforce ADMIN_ROLE, validate ranges, and never rewind the cursor
